# ============================================================
#  Club events — drawn while the club state is active.
#  Clubs are joined at the Club Fair (calendar.grim) except the
#  Midnight Cartographers, who find you.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Dueling Circle ----------------

@event duel_practice_bout
title: Practice Bout
class: routine
tone: light
track: duelling
weight: 14
art: duel
tags: club
scene: A chalk circle on a stone floor under high windows, two students mid-duel, a ring of members cheering.
text: Wednesday practice. The captain pairs you with a fourth-year who has a reputation for ending bouts quickly. "Defence or attack," the captain says. "Pick one and commit."
> left: Hold your ground
  challenge combat apprentice+ steady:
    win:
      vigor +small
      renown +small
      say: You weather everything she throws until she runs out of breath. The captain nods slowly.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: You hold your ground very bravely, right up until you're on the floor.
> right: Go on the attack
  challenge combat apprentice+ wild:
    win:
      arcana +small
      renown +small
      say: Your opening hex catches her off guard. Point to you. The circle whoops.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: She sidesteps and you hex the wall. The wall wins.

@event duel_bram_hazing
title: Initiation, Prefect-Style
class: routine
tone: tense
when: rank(duelling) == 1
track: duelling
actor: bram
weight: 12
art: shield
tags: club rival
scene: A burly upper-year in a prefect's sash blocking a corridor, wand twirling, a crowd of members watching nervously.
text: Bram Hollis, prefect and senior Circle member, has decided new members need "toughening up". He's made you hold a shield-charm against him for an hour. The hour is not up.
> left: Endure it
  meet bram
  vigor +small
  mood -small
  rel bram +small
  say: Your arms shake. You don't drop the charm. Bram grunts, almost approvingly, and finds someone else to torment.
> right: Drop the shield and duel him
  meet bram
  challenge combat vs bram.vigor:
    win:
      renown +medium
      rel bram -large
      bond bram rival
      say: You disarm him in front of everyone. His wand clatters across the floor. The silence is delicious. He will remember this.
    lose:
      health -medium
      rel bram -small
      say: Bram flattens you with a single bored flick. "Toughening up," he reminds the room.

@event duel_lyra_training
title: Training Partners
class: routine
tone: tense
when: met(lyra) and month == 6 and rel(lyra) >= 0
track: duelling
actor: lyra
weight: 14
art: duel
tags: club rival social
scene: A misty lawn at dawn, two figures practising wand forms side by side, frost on the grass.
text: Lyra finds you after practice. "The tournament is in two months. You're the only person in this club who doesn't bore me. Train with me. Dawn. Every day. Don't be late."
> left: Decline — you need sleep
  rel lyra -tiny
  say: "Sleep," she repeats, as if it's a foreign word. "Fine."
> right: Agree
  health -tiny
  gain training
  rel lyra +medium
  say: She's a merciless coach. Somewhere around the third week, you notice she's started bringing two cups of tea.

# ---------------- Choir of the Spheres ----------------

@event choir_solo
title: Solo Auditions
class: routine
tone: light
place: great_hall
weight: 14
art: music
tags: club
scene: A circular choir loft under a painted dome, a single student standing in a pool of light, the rest of the choir floating gently above their seats.
text: Auditions for the Midwinter solo. The choirmaster's eyebrows are famously hard to impress. Your throat is dry. Your hands are wet.
> left: Stay in the back row
  mood +tiny
  say: You harmonise from safety, and it's lovely. Somebody else gets the solo and cries with relief.
> right: Audition
  challenge negotiate apprentice+:
    win:
      renown +medium
      mood +small
      say: You hit the high note and the candles in the loft all flare at once. The choirmaster's eyebrows rise one millimetre. You got it.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: Your voice cracks on the high note and a candle goes out in protest.

@event choir_levitation
title: Off-Key Altitude
class: routine
tone: light
place: great_hall
weight: 14
art: music
tags: club magic
scene: A choir hovering a few feet off the floor, all in harmony — except one singer, who has dropped back to the ground with a thump.
text: The Choir of the Spheres literally floats when it harmonises. You keep falling out of the air on the third verse. People are starting to notice the thumps.
> left: Mime the hard bits
  guile +tiny
  say: Nobody notices. You float serenely, mouthing words. It's a little bit like fraud.
> right: Practise every night
  charm +small
  health -tiny
  say: A week of late nights and you float through the third verse like a feather. The choirmaster gives you a tiny nod.

@event choir_concert
title: The Winter Concert
class: routine
tone: light
when: (month == 4 or month == 5)
place: great_hall
weight: 16
art: bell
tags: club festival
scene: The great hall at night, a floating choir lit by candles, the audience below with faces tilted up.
text: The winter concert. The great hall is packed. Somewhere in the audience, the Ledger's critic is sharpening her quill.
> left: Sing for the audience
  renown +small
  mood +small
  say: You sing and the hall sways. The review calls the choir "unearthly". You cut it out and keep it.
> right: Sing for yourself
  mood +medium
  say: You close your eyes and forget anyone is listening. When you open them, you are higher than everyone else.

# ---------------- Skyrace Squad ----------------

@event sky_tryouts
title: Tryouts
class: routine
tone: light
when: not flag(sky_team)
place: flight_field
weight: 18
art: broom
tags: club
scene: Brooms streaking around the towers, hoops of light hanging in the sky, a captain with a whistle on the battlements.
text: Skyrace tryouts: three laps around the towers, through the hoops, without dying. The captain has a stopwatch and no visible sense of humour.
> left: Fly clean and steady
  challenge feat apprentice+ steady:
    win:
      flag sky_team
      find lead_sky_championship
      renown +small
      say: You're not the fastest, but you hit every hoop. "Reserve," says the captain. Then: "...no. Team."
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: You miss two hoops and nearly a gargoyle. "Reserves," says the captain. "Keep practising."
> right: Go full speed
  challenge feat apprentice+ wild:
    win:
      flag sky_team
      find lead_sky_championship
      renown +medium
      say: You scream through the hoops so fast the stopwatch has to be checked. You're on the team. Obviously.
    lose:
      health -medium
      say: You go full speed into the north tower. The tower is fine.

@event sky_crash
title: A Bad Landing
class: routine
tone: tense
place: flight_field
weight: 12
art: broom
tags: club danger
scene: A broom snapped in two on the grass, a student sitting up dazed, teammates landing around them.
text: Practice. A gust catches you mid-turn, and the ground arrives rather sooner than expected. Your ankle is making an interesting shape.
> left: Walk it off
  vigor +tiny
  chance even:
    gain injured
    say: You do not walk it off. You limp it off, for a month.
  else:
    say: Tough as old boots. The team cheers when you get back on your broom.
> right: Straight to the infirmary
  gold -tiny
  health +small
  say: Sister Amaranth sets it in a minute and charges you three crowns for "carelessness". Fair.

@event sky_championship
title: Lumenhold vs. Thornwick
class: routine
tone: light
when: flag(sky_team) and month >= 6
place: flight_field
weight: 16
art: trophy
tags: club festival
scene: Two teams of broom-riders in blue and green above a packed stadium, the golden finishing hoop glowing at the top of the highest tower.
text: The championship against Thornwick Academy. Final lap. You're neck and neck with their captain, and the golden hoop is at the top of the tallest tower.
> left: Play it safe
  renown +small
  say: Thornwick takes the hoop by a whisker. Still: second place in the region. The team carries you off the field anyway.
> right: The suicide dive
  challenge feat adept- wild:
    win:
      renown +medium
      gain famous
      mood +large
      say: You dive straight down the tower face and pull up at the last second, through the hoop. The stadium explodes.
    lose:
      health -large
      gain injured
      renown +small
      say: You dive. You miss. The crowd gasps, then cheers you anyway when you stagger up waving.

# ---------------- The Lumen Ledger ----------------

@event ledger_pie_scoop
title: The Case of the Missing Pies
class: routine
tone: light
track: lumen_ledger
actor: nessa
weight: 14
art: paper
tags: club social
scene: A cramped newspaper office in a tower attic, a printing press clanking, a girl with an ink-stained grin pointing at a map pinned with string.
text: Nessa slams a file on your desk. "Pies. Forty-two of them, gone from the kitchens in a single night. I want the culprit, I want a photo and I want it by Friday."
> left: Write a light-hearted piece
  charm +tiny
  say: "Pie-rates Strike Again." Nessa groans at the headline and prints it anyway.
> right: Actually investigate
  challenge deceive journeyman-:
    win:
      renown +small
      rel nessa +medium
      say: The culprit: a family of brownies living in the chimney. Your story runs on the front page. Nessa frames it.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      rel nessa +tiny
      say: You stake out the kitchens for three nights and catch nothing but a cold. Nessa pats your head.

@event ledger_bram_story
title: The Prefect's Bribes
class: routine
tone: tense
when: met(bram)
track: lumen_ledger
actor: nessa
weight: 12
art: scales
tags: club rival
scene: An anonymous note spread on a desk under a lamp, next to a sketch of a prefect taking a coin purse from a first-year.
text: An anonymous tip: Bram Hollis has been taking bribes from first-years to skip their demerits. You have a witness. Nessa wants your byline on it. "This is real journalism," she says, eyes shining.
> left: Kill the story
  alignment -tiny
  rel nessa -small
  rel bram +small
  say: Nessa is disappointed in you. Somehow, Bram finds out you buried it. He nods at you in the corridor. You feel slightly dirty.
> right: Publish it
  alignment +tiny
  renown +medium
  rel nessa +medium
  rel bram -large
  gain watched
  if rel(bram) < -18:
    bond bram nemesis
  say: The story runs. Bram is stripped of his sash for a month. He gets it back. And now he knows exactly who you are.

@event ledger_deadline
title: Deadline Night
class: routine
tone: light
track: lumen_ledger
actor: nessa
weight: 12
art: candle
tags: club
scene: The newspaper office at 3am, crumpled drafts on the floor, two students slumped over typesetting trays.
text: The press runs at dawn and half the paper is blank. Nessa is chewing her quill. "I need you tonight. All night. I'll owe you."
> left: Say you have revision to do
  study +tiny
  rel nessa -tiny
  say: You sleep. The paper comes out with a large drawing of a duck on page four. Nessa doesn't speak to you for a day.
> right: Pull an all-nighter
  health -small
  study -tiny
  rel nessa +medium
  say: You write three articles and a horoscope. At dawn Nessa falls asleep on your shoulder, ink on her nose.

# ---------------- Verdant Circle ----------------

@event garden_mandrakes
title: The Mandrake Choir
class: routine
tone: light
track: verdant
weight: 14
art: leaf
tags: club nature
scene: Rows of potted mandrakes in a steamy greenhouse, their little leafy heads opened in song.
text: The greenhouse mandrakes have started singing again. Off-key and enthusiastic. The earmuffs are on the hook by the door. Tobias isn't wearing his; he's harmonising.
> left: Earmuffs on
  alchemy +tiny
  say: You repot six mandrakes in blissful silence. Good honest work.
> right: Sing along
  mood +small
  chance unlikely:
    health -tiny
    say: You sing along and promptly faint. Mandrake song is strong stuff. You wake up very relaxed.
  else:
    say: The mandrakes adore you. The greenhouse sounds like a pub at closing time.

@event garden_moonflower
title: The Moonflower
class: routine
tone: warm
when: met(tobias)
track: verdant
actor: tobias
weight: 12
art: flower
tags: club romance nature
scene: A single silver flower opening in the dark of a glass greenhouse, two faces lit by its glow.
text: "The moonflower's going to bloom tonight," Tobias says, a little breathless. "Once every eleven years. I'm staying up to see it. You... could stay too. If you want."
> left: You need sleep
  rel tobias -tiny
  say: "Course. Yeah." He tells you about it at breakfast, in detail, with gestures.
> right: Stay up with him
  health -tiny
  rel tobias +medium
  spark tobias +small
  mood +small
  say: At 2am the flower opens and fills the greenhouse with silver light. Tobias doesn't look at the flower. He looks at you.

@event garden_maud_secret
title: The Secret Garden
class: routine
tone: light
when: member(verdant) or (month >= 7 and month <= 9)
actor: maud
weight: 5
art: mushroom
tags: club nature
scene: An old woman in a battered straw hat holding open a hidden door in an ivy-covered wall; beyond, impossible flowers glow.
text: The old groundskeeper beckons you behind the potting shed, to a door in the wall you've walked past a hundred times without seeing. "You've got the hands for it," Old Maud says. "Want to see what grows where nobody's looking?"
> left: Thank her and decline
  meet maud
  rel maud +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: "Suit yourself." The door is gone when you look back. You make your class with a minute to spare, oddly pleased with yourself.
> right: Follow her in
  meet maud
  rel maud +medium
  alchemy +small
  gain blessed
  study -tiny
  say: Inside: glowing ferns, silver bees, a pear tree that hums. Maud tucks a sprig of rosemary into your pocket. "For luck. Don't lose it." You lose the whole afternoon in there, and a class with it.

# ---------------- Stargazers ----------------

@event stars_cocoa_night
time: evening night
title: Cocoa on the Roof
class: routine
tone: light
place: observatory
weight: 14
art: cup
tags: club social
scene: Students wrapped in blankets on a flat roof, steaming mugs in hand, telescopes pointed at a velvet sky.
text: Stargazers meet on the roof with blankets, telescopes and an illegal quantity of cocoa. Tonight is cloudy. Nobody cares.
> left: Talk until dawn
  mood +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: You talk about home, about the future, about whether stars are lonely. Someone falls asleep on your shoulder.
> right: Do your homework by starlight
  lore +small
  study +tiny
  say: You finish your essay by the light of the cocoa-warmer charm. Productive. A little lonely.

@event stars_meteor_bet
time: evening night
title: The Meteor Wager
class: routine
tone: light
place: observatory
weight: 12
art: dice
tags: club money
scene: A chalkboard on an observatory wall covered in tally marks and names, a pile of coins on a stool beneath it.
text: The club is running a betting pool on tonight's meteor count. The current favourite is 40. The charts suggest something else. Or do they?
> left: Bet on the charts
  when: gold >= 8
  challenge research journeyman-:
    win:
      gold +medium
      say: Fifty-three meteors. You called fifty-two. Close enough to win the pot.
    lose:
      gold -small
      say: The charts were wrong, or you read them wrong. Eight crowns gone.
> right: Stay out of it
  mood +tiny
  say: You watch the meteors for their own sake. Turns out that's the best seat in the house.

@event stars_constellation
title: An Unnamed Shape
class: story
tone: eerie
place: observatory
weight: 12
art: star
tags: club mystery
scene: A star chart spread on a table, a student's finger tracing a new pattern between unmarked stars.
text: Plotting the autumn sky, you notice seven faint stars that form a ring around nothing. The charts call that patch of sky "empty". It doesn't look empty.
> left: Ignore it
  say: You plot the usual constellations. Your chart gets top marks.
  study astromancy +tiny
> right: Investigate
  lore +medium
  flag saw_hollow_star
  say: You spend a week in the archives. Three hundred years ago, the patch was called the Hollow. Then someone scraped the name off every chart.

# ---------------- Midnight Cartographers ----------------

@event carto_invite
time: evening night
title: An Invitation at Midnight
class: routine
tone: eerie
when: met(corvin) and rel(corvin) >= 6 and not member(cartographers) and turn >= 4
actor: corvin
weight: 20
art: map
tags: club mystery
scene: A slip of black paper pushed under a dormitory door, a silver ink map on it that rearranges itself as you watch.
text: A black card under your door. On it, a map in silver ink that redraws itself while you watch. Corvin's handwriting: "Midnight. Under the third gargoyle. Bring a candle. Tell no one."
> left: Ignore it
  rel corvin -tiny
  say: The card blanks itself the next morning. Corvin doesn't mention it, but he's a little cooler for a week.
> right: Go
  health -tiny
  join cartographers
  rel corvin +medium
  guile +tiny
  say: Under the gargoyle: six students, a stack of maps and a passage you'd never seen. "Welcome," says Corvin, "to the club that doesn't exist."

@event carto_thursday_stairs
title: The Thursday Staircase
class: routine
tone: eerie
slot: midnight
track: cartographers
weight: 14
art: map
tags: club mystery
scene: A spiral staircase emerging from a blank wall in moonlight, its steps unfolding one by one.
text: The Cartographers have heard of a staircase that only exists on Thursdays between midnight and one. Tonight is Thursday. It is 11:58.
> left: Map it carefully
  health -tiny
  lore +small
  guile +tiny
  say: You chart forty-one steps and a landing with a window onto a sky that isn't this one. The map is the club's pride.
> right: Climb it to the top
  challenge deceive journeyman wild:
    win:
      gold +large
      say: At the top, a forgotten storeroom. Inside: a chest of old academy coins. The club splits it. Corvin cries a little.
    lose:
      mood -small
      say: At one o'clock the staircase stops existing. You were on it. You land in a laundry chute.

@event carto_lake_tunnel
title: The Tunnel Under the Lake
class: story
tone: eerie
when: not flag(found_lake_tunnel)
track: cartographers
weight: 12
art: door
tags: club mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A narrow brick tunnel dripping with water, lit by a single candle, ending at a round door carved with a black star.
text: A loose stone in the boathouse cellar opens on a tunnel running out under the lake. The bricks drip. At the far end, a round door carved with a black star. It is warm to the touch.
> left: Mark it and leave
  flag found_lake_tunnel
  lore +tiny
  say: You add the tunnel to the club map with a skull beside it. Corvin adds a second skull, to be safe.
> right: Press your palm to the star
  flag found_lake_tunnel
  alignment -small
  arcana +small
  mood -tiny
  gain hollow_dreams
  say: The star drinks the warmth out of your hand. Behind the door, something very large shifts in its sleep.
